<title>INDIA: Indian cotton trade shut for local festival.</title>
<headline>Indian cotton trade shut for local festival.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's cotton trade was shut on Wednesday for a local religious festival, dealers said.</p>
<p>Trading will resume on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, cotton prices fell on profit-taking prompted by increased offerings from state agencies.</p>
<p>&quot;Export deals remained thin and hardly a few thousand bales were traded at the rate of 57.50/60 cents per pound,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
